<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="63af26d1-e067-537e-9604-81ffd68f8e5c" activityNameId="a5773380-b5fe-55ef-9027-4b958bc1c3fb" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Use of wireless IP access network, 2-4G per hour</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Use of wireless IP access network, 2-4G per hour
The data set represents 2-4G wireless networks in Switzerland; UUID: 91769337-e735-3336-b260-861e5562528a
The dataset is based on multiple Swisscom 2-4G sites. The equipment considered are antennas, baseband units, cooling units, indoor cabinets, lead acid battery, PSU indoor cabinet, radio units, routers, and cables. The amount of electricity consumed is calculated by multiplying the network energy intensity with the total network traffic. The network energy intensity is based on the latest information from Telefonica since the company presents updated information regarding the energy intensity (kWh/GB) of different access network types. The amount of network traffic is based on the Swisscom network. It is assumed that the devices have a lifetime of 6 years, similar to the core network and based on a blade server platform. The reference year is 2021 based on the information from Telefonica. The functional unit = 1 GB.
Location: Data for Swiss networks
Technology: The mix of Swiss access transmission network, wireless. 2-4G technologies are considered.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Literature &amp; own estimations
Extrapolations: Average technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_91769337-e735-3336-b260-861e5562528a.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
